  "question": {
    "text": "5 beats/ second are heard when a turning fork is sounded with a sonometer wire under tension, when the length of the sonometer wire is either $0.95 \\mathrm{~m}$ or $1 \\mathrm{~m}$. The frequency of the fork will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jwmfA",
      "text": "\n$195 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WbMPI",
      "text": "\n$251 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LdvfX",
      "text": "\n$150 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "knFmz",
      "text": "\n$300 \\mathrm{~Hz}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Probable frequencies of tuning fork be $n \\pm$ 5\nFrequency of sonometer wire, $n \\propto \\frac{1}{l}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\therefore \\frac{n+5}{n-5}=\\frac{100}{95} \\Rightarrow 95(n+5)=100(n-5) \\\\\n&\\text { or, } 95 n+475=100 n-500 \\\\\n&\\text { or, } 5 n=975 \\\\\n&\\text { or, } n=\\frac{975}{5}=195 \\mathrm{~Hz}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
